XR2_N g_n VSS sub! rppd w=1.0u l=14.5u m=1 b=0 mm_ok=1
XM1 cml_out_n g_p e_cmos VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=6.0u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XM2 cml_out_p g_n e_cmos VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=6.0u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XMTAIL e_cmos VDD VSS VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=2.5u l=0.50u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XM3 cml_out_n VLOAD VDD VDD sg13_lv_pmos w=16.0u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
* C122: symmetric cml load - XM4 changed from the mirror (gate
* cml_out_n) to a MATCHED DIODE-CONNECTED load (gate cml_out_p), so
* cml_out_p and cml_out_n swing equally about a common level. The
* C120/C121 latch experiments were fed a full-swing signal against a
* near-constant 0.65 V bias node (cml_out_n is the diode side of the
* mirror) - the latch was fed the wrong thing, not refuted. With the
* true pair, feed the C121 precharged latch unchanged.
XM4 cml_out_p VLOAD VDD VDD sg13_lv_pmos w=16.0u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
* C148: CMFB acting on the LOAD, not the tail. The C146 loop changed
* two things at once (cm AND tail current) - it refuted "cm alone is
* sufficient" but never raised cm with the current held. Here the
* diode pmos gates are servoed to hold cm at 0.75 V (gate = VLOAD, the
* loop output), XMTAIL stays FIXED at 2.5u with its gate at VDD - cm
* and tail current become independent. Amp and sense as C146
* (first-order, stated): XCMR1/2 rppd w=1.0u l=40u, VCMREF 0.75 V
* ideal, XCMT/XCMA/XCMB/XCMP1/2 w=2.0u/1.0u. Polarity: cm_sense >
* ref -> VLOAD up -> loads weaker -> cm down.
XCMR1 cml_out_p cm_sense sub! rppd w=1.0u l=40u m=1 b=0 mm_ok=1
XCMR2 cml_out_n cm_sense sub! rppd w=1.0u l=40u m=1 b=0 mm_ok=1
VCMREF cm_ref 0 0.75
XCMT e_cm VDD VSS VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=2.0u l=0.50u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XCMA a cm_sense e_cm VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=1.0u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XCMB VLOAD cm_ref e_cm VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=1.0u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XCMP1 a a VDD VDD sg13_lv_pmos w=2.0u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XCMP2 VLOAD a VDD VDD sg13_lv_pmos w=2.0u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1

XCDAMP1 cml_out_p VSS cap_cmim w=2.0u l=2.0u m=1 mm_ok=1
XCDAMP2 cml_out_n VSS cap_cmim w=2.0u l=2.0u m=1 mm_ok=1
* C120: clocked regenerative latch (sense-amp) replacing XM5/XM6/XRFB
* Sense amp evaluates on CLK_N high (the comparator's latch phase, when
* the cml differential is settled): tail XSA_T, input pair XSA1/XSA2
* (gates cml_out_p/cml_out_n), cross-coupled pmos XSA3/XSA4 and nmos
* XSA5/XSA6 - the sense nodes regenerate to the rails. Hold latch
* XHL1/XHL1N/XHL2/XHL2N (cross-coupled inverters) holds raw_inv/sa_n
* between strobes. raw_inv = NOT(cml_out_p) polarity preserved; XM7
* through XM10 unchanged.
* Sizing PROVISIONAL first-order (STATED, not fitted): input pair
* w=2.0u (XM6 geometry), cross-coupled pmos w=2.83u (XM5 geometry),
* cross-coupled nmos w=2.0u, tail w=4.0u.
XSA_T e_sa SACLK VSS VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=4.0u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XSA1 raw_inv cml_out_p e_sa VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=2.0u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XSA2 sa_n cml_out_n e_sa VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=2.0u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XSA3 raw_inv sa_n VDD VDD sg13_lv_pmos w=2.83u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XSA4 sa_n raw_inv VDD VDD sg13_lv_pmos w=2.83u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XSA5 raw_inv sa_n e_sa VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=2.0u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XSA6 sa_n raw_inv e_sa VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=2.0u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
* C125: hold latch MOVED OFF the sense nodes - the C120 spec put
* precharge and hold on the same two nodes, they fought, and the hold
* won on sa_n (never wiped; +0.4815 V mean strobe-start imbalance vs a
* 0.10 V input differential - the latch was 480 mV pre-committed).
* Now: raw_inv/sa_n carry ONLY precharge (XPC1/XPC2, CLK_N low) and the
* sense amp - no hold devices, turbulent. The cross-coupled hold latch
* sits AFTER the buffers on the separate raw_buf/sa_buf pair, which is
* what XM7 reads (sa_buf, polarity preserved).
* C127: NAND2 SR latch - the sense amp is a StrongARM (both sense
* nodes precharge HIGH, exactly one falls on evaluate) - self-timed
* for a cross-coupled NAND SR with active-low inputs: both high
* (precharge) = HOLD, one falling = SET. No write window, no strength
* fight (NAND inputs are gates; the sense amp drives pure capacitance).
* Q = NAND(raw_inv, qbar), qbar = NAND(sa_n, Q). XM7 reads Q.
* Minimum size w=0.5u l=0.13u, STATED not fitted.
XN1P1 Q raw_inv VDD VDD sg13_lv_pmos w=0.5u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XN1P2 Q qbar VDD VDD sg13_lv_pmos w=0.5u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XN1N1 Q raw_inv n1a VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=0.5u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XN1N2 n1a qbar VSS VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=0.5u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XN2P1 qbar sa_n VDD VDD sg13_lv_pmos w=0.5u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XN2P2 qbar Q VDD VDD sg13_lv_pmos w=0.5u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XN2N1 qbar sa_n n2a VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=0.5u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XN2N2 n2a Q VSS VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=0.5u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
* C121: precharge pmos - pull raw_inv and sa_n to VDD while CLK_N is low
* (gate=CLK_N), so each strobe starts with both sense nodes clean at
* VDD (the C120 latch regenerated once and never released - no
* precharge). Sized strong (w=6.0u) to override the hold latch,
* PROVISIONAL first-order, STATED not fitted.
XPC1 raw_inv SACLK VDD VDD sg13_lv_pmos w=6.0u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XPC2 sa_n SACLK VDD VDD sg13_lv_pmos w=6.0u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
* C123: buffer the latch. raw_inv carries XM7-XM10 (four gates) while
* sa_n carries nothing - identical precharge devices, asymmetric load,
* so raw_inv floors at ~0.675 V and the latch cannot pull it down.
* Fix: minimum-size inverter on raw_inv (BUF_R) and on sa_n (BUF_S);
* the latch now sees only the two buffer gates. XM7-XM10 are driven
* from sa_buf = NOT(sa_n) = raw_inv-sense (the cross-coupling makes
* NOT(sa_n) equal to raw_inv's polarity), so the chain polarity is
* preserved: PBIT_OUT = NOT(sa_n) = raw_inv as in the original.
* Buffer size w=0.5u (minimum-class), STATED not fitted.
* C133: two-inverter buffer between Q and XM7 - the 0.5u NAND cannot
* drive XM7's 2.83u/2.0u gates inside the 100 ps evaluate (Q maxed at
* 0.297 V, never a logic high). Buffer: stage 1 pmos 0.8u / nmos 0.6u,
* stage 2 pmos 2.4u / nmos 1.8u, non-inverting (polarity preserved:
* QBUF = Q), NAND left at minimum size so the latch stays fast.
* Sizes STATED, not fitted.
XB1P QBUF1 Q VDD VDD sg13_lv_pmos w=0.5u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XB1N QBUF1 Q VSS VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=0.35u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XB2P QBUF QBUF1 VDD VDD sg13_lv_pmos w=1.14u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XB2N QBUF QBUF1 VSS VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=0.81u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XM7 PBIT_RAW QBUF VDD VDD sg13_lv_pmos w=2.61u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XM8 PBIT_RAW QBUF VSS VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=1.86u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XM9 PBIT_OUT PBIT_RAW VDD VDD sg13_lv_pmos w=5.98u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XM10 PBIT_OUT PBIT_RAW VSS VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=4.27u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XM11 CLK_OUT_DIV CLK_P VDD VDD sg13_lv_pmos w=2.83u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XM12 CLK_OUT_DIV CLK_P VSS VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=2.0u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
* V7 MERGE: 2-binary (codes 0-3) + 150 unary elements of 4 LSB (codes 4-603).
* 603 codes, 151 handovers, segmenting at b1. Handover = code 3->4 = VCODE 0.03->0.04.
* NO 1.037u compensation encoded (H-742 one-draw artifact); mechanism = delta-VBE =
* kT/q*ln4 at the unary current sources; re-tune on the ensemble targeting x=1.03.
XQU1 vsegu1 c_p1_comp e_dacu1 sub! npn13G2 Nx=4 mm_ok=1
XRCU1 e_dacu1 VSS sub! rppd w=1.0u l=5.4u m=4 b=0 mm_ok=1
XSWUP1 c_p ubar1 vsegu1 VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=2.0u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XSWUN1 c_n u1 vsegu1 VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=2.0u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XQU2 vsegu2 c_p1_comp e_dacu2 sub! npn13G2 Nx=4 mm_ok=1
XRCU2 e_dacu2 VSS sub! rppd w=1.0u l=5.4u m=4 b=0 mm_ok=1
XSWUP2 c_p ubar2 vsegu2 VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=2.0u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XSWUN2 c_n u2 vsegu2 VSS sg13_lv_nmos w=2.0u l=0.13u ng=1 m=1 mm_ok=1
XQU3 vsegu3 c_p1_comp e_dacu3 sub! npn13G2 Nx=4 mm_ok=1
